  "reason": "The current best (config_035: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc 0.725) shows that scvi_n200 dramatically outperforms pca_n2000 (~10 pt gap), and weighted+transformer is the best aggregation/fusion combo. However, scgpt has never been tested in multimodal settings with the best aggregation/fusion configuration. config_044 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is a clean A/B comparison against config_035, isolating the RNA encoder as the only variable. This is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve: if scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction for the remaining 3 experiments; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 is optimal and lets us focus remaining budget on fine-tuning around the current best. With 3 experiments left, resolving this key design choice now is more informative than testing lower-priority variations (e.g., concat fusion or resnet50) that are less likely to beat 0.725."
